 confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-yxzgqu0R' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-04 14:08:07.998 xcodebuild[61532:108896430]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-04 14:08:08.190 xcodebuild[61532:108896429] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n0ecddf87e313202bd41aef3ac657bd4294fdc9fb\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-D5smlKqD' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-04 14:08:09.446 xcodebuild[61540:108896469]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-04 14:08:09.624 xcodebuild[61540:108896468] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-TjhAXafj' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-04 14:08:10.169 xcodebuild[61544:108896512]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-04 14:08:10.347 xcodebuild[61544:108896511] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc                  | 148 +++++++++++++++++++---------\n src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc          |  26 +++--\n src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc |   6 +-\n test/yang/call/conformance.clj              |  16 +--\n test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj               |  49 +++++++++\n 5 files changed, 178 insertions(+), 67 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\nindex 4f0d9e74..f24c14eb 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n@@ -1200,6 +1200,23 @@\n        (not (contains? (::defined env) operator))))\n \n \n+(defn- cell-ref-shaped-node\n+  \"The UAST test that the callee node carries an authentic cell\n+   reference's shape: `:type :cell-ref` with the `:id` and `:seal`\n+   every issued reference carries. A source map spelled\n+   `{:type :cell-ref}` carries neither and is ordinary data; a map\n+   spelling the full shape with a forged id or seal still reaches\n+   `cell/get`, where the VM's seal refuses it.\"\n+  [callee]\n+  (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n+                    (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) callee (u/lit :type))\n+                    (u/lit :cell-ref))\n+             (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/contains?) callee (u/lit :id))\n+                        (u/app (u/v 'data/contains?) callee (u/lit :seal))\n+                        (u/lit false))\n+             (u/lit false)))\n+\n+\n (defn- compile-guest-call\n   \"Admit a source operator before common invocation. Only generated UAST\n    implementation calls apply private closures directly.\"\n@@ -1310,9 +1327,7 @@\n                      (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/map?) (u/v callee))\n                                 (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/contains?) (u/v callee) (u/lit :yang.call/entry))\n                                            (u/lit true)\n-                                           (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n-                                                  (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v callee) (u/lit :type))\n-                                                  (u/lit :cell-ref)))\n+                                           (cell-ref-shaped-node (u/v callee)))\n                                 (u/lit false))\n                      admitted\n                      value-call)\n@@ -2103,27 +2118,52 @@\n                            (u/sexp->uast\n                              '(fn [dsg__candidate]\n                                 (if (data/map? dsg__candidate)\n-                                  (if (dsg__equal (dsg__get dsg__candidate :type)\n-                                                  :cell-ref)\n-                                    ;; A cell-backed callable stores its entry\n-                                    ;; in the cell contents (yang.antlr.md\n-                                    ;; 8.10.2); projection is structural, as\n-                                    ;; `yang.call/_descriptor` projects it.\n-                                    ;; Only the cell case dereferences, so a\n-                                    ;; source map with an entry spelling\n-                                    ;; still needs the witness below.\n-                                    (let [dsg__descriptor (cell/get dsg__candidate)\n-                                          dsg__entry (dsg__get dsg__descriptor\n-                                                               :yang.call/entry)]\n-                                      (data/callable? dsg__entry))\n-                                    (let [dsg__entry (dsg__get dsg__candidate :yang.call/entry)\n-                                          dsg__witness (dsg__get dsg__candidate :clj/admission)]\n-                                      (if (data/callable? dsg__entry)\n-                                        (dsg__equal\n-                                          dsg__witness\n-                                          (dsg__make_admission\n-                                            (dsg__assoc dsg__candidate :clj/admission nil)))\n-                                        false)))\n+                                  ;; An authentic cell reference carries\n+                                  ;; the `:id` and `:seal` the VM issued\n+                                  ;; it with; only that shape is\n+                                  ;; dereferenced, as the descriptor\n+                                  ;; projection does for a cell-backed\n+                                  ;; callable (yang.antlr.md 8.10.2),\n+                                  ;; whose entry lives in the cell\n+                                  ;; contents. A source map spelled\n+                                  ;; `{:type :cell-ref}` carries\n+                                  ;; neither: it falls to the witness\n+                                  ;; branch and, entryless, is no more\n+                                  ;; admitted than any other source\n+                                  ;; map. A forged full shape still\n+                                  ;; reaches `cell/get`, where the VM\n+                                  ;; seal refuses it.\n+                                  (let [dsg__cell-ref?\n+                                        (if (dsg__equal\n+                                              (dsg__get dsg__candidate :type)\n+                                              :cell-ref)\n+                                          (if (data/contains? dsg__candidate\n+                                                              :id)\n+                                            (data/contains? dsg__candidate\n+                                                            :seal)\n+                                            false)\n+                                          false)]\n+                                    (if dsg__cell-ref?\n+                                      (let [dsg__descriptor\n+                                            (cell/get dsg__candidate)\n+                                            dsg__entry\n+                                            (dsg__get dsg__descriptor\n+                                                      :yang.call/entry)]\n+                                        (data/callable? dsg__entry))\n+                                      (let [dsg__entry\n+                                            (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n+                                                      :yang.call/entry)\n+                                            dsg__witness\n+                                            (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n+                                                      :clj/admission)]\n+                                        (if (data/callable? dsg__entry)\n+                                          (dsg__equal\n+                                            dsg__witness\n+                                            (dsg__make_admission\n+                                              (dsg__assoc dsg__candidate\n+                                                          :clj/admission\n+                                                          nil)))\n+                                          false))))\n                                   false))))\n          (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__make_entry (call-entry))\n          (outcomes? env) (u/let1\n@@ -2712,13 +2752,18 @@\n   \"Rewrite the compiled `node` for the linked unit: a top-level\n    definition in `names` becomes a `clj/define-global!` write and a free\n    read of one becomes a `clj/global-get`, both under the name's string.\n-   A store definition inside the unit thunk is conditional to the\n-   linker, so no body read of it discharges (the runtime preludes avoid\n-   this by keeping every definition at module level); the runtime\n-   global namespace is the linked unit's definition table instead, as\n-   a Python module body writes its dictionary. Lexically bound names,\n-   quoted literals and macro definitions keep their store shape: a\n-   macro is not a runtime value.\"\n+   The `names` a unit is lowered with are its own top-level definitions,\n+   its guest library's and the projected names the composition bound in\n+   the runtime global namespace, so a projected export and a definition\n+   read through the one binding: a definition the unit itself runs\n+   publishes after the projection and shadows it. A store definition\n+   inside the unit thunk is conditional to the linker, so no body read\n+   of it discharges (the runtime preludes avoid this by keeping every\n+   definition at module level); the runtime global namespace is the\n+   linked unit's definition table instead, as a Python module body\n+   writes its dictionary. Lexically bound names, quoted literals and\n+   macro definitions keep their store shape: a macro is not a runtime\n+   value.\"\n   [node names bound]\n   (case (:type node)\n     :literal node\n@@ -2762,24 +2807,29 @@\n    the guest library they need, compiled unmodified under `unit-opts`\n    and published to the runtime global namespace by\n    `publish-to-globals` — so the helper's export projection can read\n-   each top-level definition. The program's own `yang.call` call sites\n-   need no free-name declaration: the convention preamble\n-   `compile-program` emits defines those names locally, and the donor\n-   publication pins the `yang.call` module for the qualified reads\n-   that remain.\"\n-  [forms]\n-  (let [source (vec forms)\n-        library (library-for source)\n-        program (compile-program (concat source library) true unit-opts)\n-        macros (into #{}\n-                     (comp (filter #(and (seq? %) (= 'defmacro (first %))))\n-                           (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second)))\n-                     (concat source library))\n-        names (reduce disj\n-                      (into (set (top-level-names source))\n-                            (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second) library))\n-                      macros)]\n-    (u/lam [] (publish-to-globals program names #{}))))\n+   each top-level definition. The two-argument form also takes the\n+   projected `exports` (names the composition already bound in the\n+   runtime global namespace): their free reads publish the same way, so\n+   the projection is the caller's binding for them. The program's own\n+   `yang.call` call sites need no free-name declaration: the convention\n+   preamble `compile-program` emits defines those names locally, and\n+   the donor publication pins the `yang.call` module for the qualified\n+   reads that remain.\"\n+  ([forms] (lower-unit forms []))\n+  ([forms exports]\n+   (let [source (vec forms)\n+         library (library-for source)\n+         program (compile-program (concat source library) true unit-opts)\n+         macros (into #{}\n+                      (comp (filter #(and (seq? %) (= 'defmacro (first %))))\n+                            (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second)))\n+                      (concat source library))\n+         names (reduce disj\n+                       (into (set (top-level-names source))\n+                             (concat (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second) library)\n+                                     (map symbol exports)))\n+                       macros)]\n+     (u/lam [] (publish-to-globals program names #{})))))\n \n \n (defn output\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\nindex ca8556dd..42a3bead 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\n@@ -7,18 +7,25 @@\n \n    Three surfaces, mirroring the other runtimes:\n \n-   - the entry, `clj/run-main`: initialize the runtime state, reset the\n-     global namespace (it is task-local), run the unit — the thunk\n-     `yang.clojure/lower-unit` lowered — and answer the program's value\n-     with the outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]` wrapper removed, since\n-     that wrapper is frontend-internal;\n+   - the entry, `clj/run-main`: initialize the runtime state, run the\n+     unit — the thunk `yang.clojure/lower-unit` lowered — and answer the\n+     program's value with the outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]`\n+     wrapper removed, since that wrapper is frontend-internal. The\n+     entry does not reset the global namespace: the namespace lives for\n+     the task, so a projection the composition bound between two\n+     entries and a definition an earlier unit published both survive\n+     into the next unit's run (as `js/run-main` leaves `globalThis`\n+     standing);\n    - the runtime global namespace, `clj/define-global!` and\n      `clj/global-get`: a task-local map in a cell (`clj.rt/globals`,\n      allocated once per task by `clj/init!`), keyed by export name. A\n      program's top-level definitions land here through its unit's own\n-     publishing, and the conformance helper's export projection reads and\n-     writes it — the JS `globalThis` table, the PHP named-function table\n-     and the Python module dictionary are the same seam;\n+     publishing, and the conformance helper's export projection reads\n+     and writes it — the one binding a linked unit reads a projected or\n+     defined name through. A definition a unit runs publishes after\n+     any projection of the same name and shadows it. The JS\n+     `globalThis` table, the PHP named-function table and the Python\n+     module dictionary are the same seam;\n    - admission, `admit`: the registry surface a linked clojure composition\n      needs beside the others — the `kind` module and the `portable`\n      adapters of the data exports the guest library's collection\n@@ -84,10 +91,11 @@\n            (data/nth value 1)\n            value)\n          value))]\n+    ;; The global namespace is the task's, not the entry's: no reset\n+    ;; here, so projections and earlier units' definitions survive.\n     [clj/run-main\n      (fn [body]\n        (do (clj/init!)\n-           (cell/set! clj.rt/globals {})\n            (clj/unwrap-outcome (body))))]])\n \n \ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\nindex d820bb60..22d34b8f 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\n@@ -137,7 +137,1