ljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2732:          (let [id (check-ref! state :cell/set! :cell-ref (:cell effect))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2733:            {:state (heap-write state id (get-in state [:heap id :seal])\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:1538:        :cell-ref (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :cell {:yin.k/hint (:id x)})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:257:(defn initial\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/code.cljc:601:(defn- definite-assignment\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/code.cljc:618:(defn- exclusive-definitions\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:379:;; `:cell-ref` (Architect cell ruling, slice 1). These are pure effect\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:678:Runtime-allocated mutable locations are not AST nodes. They are the `cell` host module's `cell/new`, `cell/get` and `cell/set!`, ordinary applications whose effects the engine interprets on all four VMs. `cell/new` answers a sealed `{:type :cell-ref :id :cell-N :seal s}`; the content lives in the task's `:heap` (see `state.md`), never in the named store.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:119:**Type:** `:heap` is `{cell-id {:value v :seal s}}`; `:gc` is `{:since n :base b :threshold t :pinned #{cell-id}}`\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:121:**Purpose:** `:heap` holds the task's cells, the mutable locations `cell/new` allocates and a sealed `:cell-ref` reaches. It is VM state, not continuation state: a write is seen by every holder of the ref and survives continuation re-entry (box semantics). `:gc` is its collector's state. Both are declared record fields wherever a VM is a positional record, and both start empty in every constructor and `spawn-module` child.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:479:(defn capture-states [initial-state ast]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/scan.cljc:51:(defn definition-occurrences\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:340:(defn- definition-at\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:356:(defn- definition-paths\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:482:(defn definitions\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/frame.cljc:69:                      (and (map? x) (contains? #{:stream-ref :cursor-ref :cell-ref} (:type x)))))]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The globals change removes the duplicate task-store binding and preserves the runtime namespace across entries. I’ve also found that the new cell test checks key presence rather than authenticity; I’m tracing its consequences and the regression coverage before issuing the verdict."}}
